WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.286
<v Casey Nguyen>Let's do the full roundup before end of week. Jordan, start with Northfield and Ferro & Vance.</v>

00:00:07.986 --> 00:00:30.700
<v Jordan Ruiz>Northfield closed at 12% off a 3-year term, onboarding's gone smoothly, on track for an October 10th go-live, and Riley's already got a QBR and a second-region upsell conversation lined up for October. Ferro & Vance closed in August, small SMB deal, stable since, a couple of routine support tickets but nothing concerning.</v>

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.543
<v Casey Nguyen>Good. Alex, Baymark and Orbis?</v>

00:00:34.243 --> 00:01:12.386
<v Alex Chen>Baymark re-engaged this week — their Q4 budget came through, Daniel wants a broader team demo the first week of October, and security already signed off back in August, so this should move faster than a typical enterprise healthcare deal once it restarts. Orbis had their CISO security review last week, went well, Marcus is satisfied pending some pen-test remediation evidence Devon's sending over, and it's moving to legal and contract review next. That one's still six-plus weeks out given their vendor risk process, but it's progressing, not stalled.</v>

00:01:13.086 --> 00:01:21.229
<v Casey Nguyen>That's a strong Q4 setup on both. What about the two losses this period — any patterns worth flagging?</v>

00:01:21.929 --> 00:01:41.214
<v Alex Chen>Kestrel Freight went to a competitor specifically over real-time streaming — we're batch-only today, and it was a hard requirement for them. Pricing wasn't the issue. I think that's worth flagging to product, it's not the first time streaming's come up in a logistics deal.</v>

00:01:41.914 --> 00:01:55.200
<v Jordan Ruiz>Vantage Foods was pure timing, they'd already signed a two-year deal with a competitor the month before we called. Nothing actionable there beyond a nurture touch closer to their 2028 renewal.</v>

00:01:55.900 --> 00:02:09.614
<v Casey Nguyen>Agreed on both reads. Alex, send the Kestrel feedback to Priya directly — if we're losing multiple logistics deals to the same gap, that's worth product knowing about concretely, not just anecdotally.</v>

00:02:10.314 --> 00:02:11.171
<v Alex Chen>Will do.</v>

00:02:11.871 --> 00:02:26.871
<v Casey Nguyen>Good week overall — one renewal saved despite a rough incident, one new logo live and stable heading into peak season, and two strong enterprise deals progressing. Let's keep the same focus into next week.</v>
